WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.500
This is the captain from the bridge.

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:10.120
41 people have been tested
positive for coronavirus.

00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:12.980
It's never gonna happen to
me, couldn't happen to me.

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:15.791
That's what me and my friends
were saying on the ship.

00:00:15.791 --> 00:00:19.560
All guest please stay
inside your staterooms

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:21.873
and do not go outside of your staterooms.

00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:25.080
You just feel desperate
when you're at sea.

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:27.490
Who's gonna let us disembark?

00:00:27.490 --> 00:00:30.140
I don't think that they
were terribly transparent

00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:32.090
about what they knew when they knew it.

00:00:33.410 --> 00:00:36.260
Carnival is, of course,
the biggest cruise company

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:39.020
in the world and since this began,

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:41.510
their ships, more than any other company's

00:00:41.510 --> 00:00:44.700
have been struck by
these outbreaks of COVID

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:45.533
on board.

00:00:45.533 --> 00:00:47.100
Hundreds of passengers on these ships

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:49.780
have been infected and
some have even died.

00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:52.410
And Bloomberg Business Week
has been reporting in depth

00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:55.140
on what went wrong and
what's next for Carnival

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:57.440
navigating this very challenging crisis.

00:01:09.940 --> 00:01:12.000
On February 3rd, the Diamond Princess

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:14.370
was around the coast of Japan.

00:01:14.370 --> 00:01:16.710
It had made stops in Hong Kong,

00:01:16.710 --> 00:01:18.973
it had gone to Taiwan and elsewhere.

00:01:20.030 --> 00:01:21.840
It was suppose to be our
last night on the cruise.

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:24.500
We were suppose to get
off the next morning.

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:27.590
Around 6:30 that night,
an announcement comes

00:01:27.590 --> 00:01:28.720
throughout the entire ship.

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:31.586
A Hong Kong resident,

00:01:31.586 --> 00:01:33.830
who traveled for five
days on Diamond Princess

00:01:33.830 --> 00:01:38.578
from Yokohama to Hong Kong
tested positive for coronavirus.

00:01:38.578 --> 00:01:40.540
Dear God.
As you can see,

00:01:40.540 --> 00:01:44.460
ladies and gentlemen, the
situation is under control

00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:47.750
and therefore, there are
no reasons for concerns.

00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:50.290
That's really when we
knew that we probably

00:01:50.290 --> 00:01:52.690
were not getting off the
ship that next morning.

00:01:54.050 --> 00:01:55.600
So, the ship cruises toward Japan

00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:59.380
and finally anchors in the
evening of February 3rd.

00:01:59.380 --> 00:02:02.360
At that point, Carnival says
the Japanese health officials

00:02:02.360 --> 00:02:04.860
came aboard and started
doing temperature checks,

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:06.150
health screening.

00:02:06.150 --> 00:02:07.900
Unfortunately, according to passengers

00:02:07.900 --> 00:02:10.490
this wasn't a really serious quarantine.

00:02:10.490 --> 00:02:13.320
Passengers said that they were
free to go about the ship.

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:14.850
My cabin mate and the other two guys

00:02:14.850 --> 00:02:18.295
that we were traveling with
were in the cabin next door.

00:02:18.295 --> 00:02:20.920
They went out and they had
a grand ole time that day.

00:02:20.920 --> 00:02:22.970
You know, as most people do.

00:02:22.970 --> 00:02:26.710
Eating in the restaurants,
watching the live house bands.

00:02:26.710 --> 00:02:28.900
Eventually, they find out
that there is actually

00:02:28.900 --> 00:02:30.271
cause for concern.

00:02:30.271 --> 00:02:33.170
The Ministry of Health has notified us

00:02:33.170 --> 00:02:38.170
that 10 people have tested
positive for coronavirus.

00:02:38.714 --> 00:02:42.936
All guest return to their
cabin and remain there

00:02:42.936 --> 00:02:44.580
for the time being.

00:02:44.580 --> 00:02:47.670
We have confirmed 10 positive cases

00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:51.560
and based on this, we
are going to quarantine

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:54.620
the entire ship for a minimum of 14 days.

00:02:54.620 --> 00:02:56.483
So, that's when it officially began.

00:03:00.310 --> 00:03:02.880
We are currently in the middle of day two

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:05.470
of the 14 day long quarantine.

00:03:05.470 --> 00:03:07.060
It is currently day three.

00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:10.270
Apparently, 41 new cases on the ship.

00:03:10.270 --> 00:03:13.290
There are 38 new people
who have tested positive.

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:15.710
44 new cases.

00:03:15.710 --> 00:03:20.710
66 additional positive
cases of coronavirus.

00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:25.280
We continued to see the
numbers go every single day.

00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:27.093
It was an emotional roller coaster.

00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:30.760
In the end, more than
700 people were infected

00:03:30.760 --> 00:03:34.190
and tragically, at least
11 people ended up dying

00:03:34.190 --> 00:03:36.650
and this was just the
beginning of the crisis

00:03:36.650 --> 00:03:37.963
for this company.

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:44.660
I wanna highlight one
of the most impressive

00:03:44.660 --> 00:03:46.150
turnover stories of our year.

00:03:46.150 --> 00:03:49.140
If not the most impressive turnaround.

00:03:49.140 --> 00:03:50.590
I'm talking about Carnival CCL.

00:03:50.590 --> 00:03:52.020
The world's largest cruise line.

00:03:52.020 --> 00:03:53.690
Are you bigger than the U.S. Navy?

00:03:54.690 --> 00:03:55.730
You know, that's a good question.

00:03:55.730 --> 00:03:58.330
I never compared number of
the ships but I doubt it.

00:04:00.430 --> 00:04:02.530
The cruise industry is really massive.

00:04:02.530 --> 00:04:04.740
Carnival Cruise, they say they see about

00:04:04.740 --> 00:04:06.620
13 million people annually.

00:04:06.620 --> 00:04:08.730
This is a booming market.

00:04:08.730 --> 00:04:10.460
People love to cruise.

00:04:10.460 --> 00:04:13.200
We've probably done two dozen cruises.

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:15.000
Sometimes we've done
two or three in a year

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:15.833
if we're lucky.

00:04:15.833 --> 00:04:18.510
Cruises are the perfect
combination between

00:04:18.510 --> 00:04:23.350
being convenient, being
affordable, and allowing you

00:04:23.350 --> 00:04:24.510
to just relax,

00:04:24.510 --> 00:04:26.460
You pack once, you unpack once.

00:04:26.460 --> 00:04:30.200
Your hotel moves with you,
your restaurant moves with you.

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:31.670
Carnival is specifically, they own about

00:04:31.670 --> 00:04:34.240
30 or 50% of the market.

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:37.330
Their annual revenue amounts
to about 20 billion dollars

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:44.480
More recently, Carnival has
run has run into some troubles.

00:04:44.480 --> 00:04:47.510
You might have seen in
the news in the 2010s.

00:04:47.510 --> 00:04:50.560
They had a boat that
capsized and actually sunk.

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:52.133
Killing about 30 people.

00:04:53.280 --> 00:04:56.190
And then later on, they had
a very high-profile incident

00:04:56.190 --> 00:04:58.280
in which they lost power on the ship

00:04:58.280 --> 00:04:59.880
and none of the plumping worked.

00:05:01.650 --> 00:05:04.800
But under Arnold Donald, who
is the current CEO of Carnival,

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:07.050
they've undergone a remarkable turnaround

00:05:07.050 --> 00:05:09.080
since about 2013.

00:05:09.080 --> 00:05:12.630
The more we give people
the opportunity to connect

00:05:12.630 --> 00:05:15.380
and experience the world together,

00:05:15.380 --> 00:05:18.010
the more spectacular our world will be.

00:05:18.010 --> 00:05:20.210
You saw the market Cap
in the first five years

00:05:20.210 --> 00:05:21.150
under of his tenure,

00:05:21.150 --> 00:05:24.480
essentially doubled to
about 50 billion dollars.

00:05:24.480 --> 00:05:26.440
Ironically, leading into this whole crisis

00:05:26.440 --> 00:05:28.850
that we've seen, you had Arnold Donald

00:05:28.850 --> 00:05:30.970
promising that he was
actually gonna correct things,

00:05:30.970 --> 00:05:34.220
he had a plan in place to
fix all these shortcuts

00:05:34.220 --> 00:05:36.600
that Carnival had
historically been taking.

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:39.120
Our task, our mission, double digit return

00:05:39.120 --> 00:05:40.500
investment cap in the
next three, four years.

00:05:40.500 --> 00:05:43.940
Well, I wanna congratulate
you on the textbook turn.

00:05:43.940 --> 00:05:45.453
The whole trend has been up.

00:05:51.970 --> 00:05:53.610
After the Diamond Princess ship,

00:05:53.610 --> 00:05:56.170
about a month passes
and then another ship,

00:05:56.170 --> 00:05:58.100
the Grand Princess, they
deal with essentially

00:05:58.100 --> 00:05:59.153
the same crisis.

00:06:01.430 --> 00:06:05.240
We boarded the ship in San Francisco and.

00:06:05.240 --> 00:06:07.850
We did think there would
be a little more enhanced

00:06:07.850 --> 00:06:09.800
screening because of what had happened

00:06:09.800 --> 00:06:11.168
on the Diamond Princess.

00:06:11.168 --> 00:06:13.990
At a minimum, we thought
they would have at least

00:06:13.990 --> 00:06:17.660
taken our temperature
as we boarded the ship

00:06:17.660 --> 00:06:20.010
but that never happened.

00:06:20.010 --> 00:06:23.910
And things just kind of
exploded on our way home.

00:06:23.910 --> 00:06:26.790
The first test are in and the coronavirus

00:06:26.790 --> 00:06:28.810
is onboard the Grand Princess.

00:06:28.810 --> 00:06:31.530
The Coast Guard delivered
test in dramatic fashion.

00:06:31.530 --> 00:06:34.620
And 21 people tested position for virus.

00:06:34.620 --> 00:06:36.360
It just kind of escalated--

00:06:36.360 --> 00:06:38.150
Quickly.
Quickly.

00:06:38.150 --> 00:06:42.300
They, you know, sequestered
us and delivered food to us

00:06:42.300 --> 00:06:45.320
in our rooms, and obviously,
that was a major shock

00:06:45.320 --> 00:06:47.730
of something's wrong.

00:06:47.730 --> 00:06:49.840
So, like the Diamond Princess in Japan,

00:06:49.840 --> 00:06:51.800
which they sailed
immediately back to port,

00:06:51.800 --> 00:06:53.760
the Grand Princess headed
back to their home port

00:06:53.760 --> 00:06:55.090
of San Francisco.

00:06:55.090 --> 00:06:57.780
3,500 people stuck in that
cruise ship off the coast

00:06:57.780 --> 00:07:01.170
of California, they will
finally be coming ashore.

00:07:01.170 --> 00:07:02.900
All passengers and crew

00:07:02.900 --> 00:07:05.820
will be tested for the coronavirus.

00:07:05.820 --> 00:07:09.840
Those that need to be
quarantined will be quarantined.

00:07:09.840 --> 00:07:12.060
In the end, it proved
a much smaller outbreak

00:07:12.060 --> 00:07:13.050
than the Diamond Princess,

00:07:13.050 --> 00:07:15.100
but that's most likely
because not everyone chose

00:07:15.100 --> 00:07:16.220
to get tested.

00:07:16.220 --> 00:07:19.280
In the end, more than 130
people tested positive.

00:07:19.280 --> 00:07:21.433
And at least five passed away.

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:28.410
As these issues are happening
aboard the Grand Princess,

00:07:28.410 --> 00:07:31.560
another ship owned by a
different Carnival Cruise line,

00:07:31.560 --> 00:07:35.690
which is Holland America
Zaandam, is sailing around.

00:07:35.690 --> 00:07:38.880
The cruise basically set sail,

00:07:38.880 --> 00:07:41.970
more or less the same day
that the U.S. State Department

00:07:41.970 --> 00:07:44.593
warned people not to be going on cruises.

00:07:45.725 --> 00:07:49.250
And the company just forged
ahead with the cruise.

00:07:49.250 --> 00:07:51.450
For some reason, they
decided to keep going.

00:08:02.350 --> 00:08:04.370
Life was good that first week.

00:08:04.370 --> 00:08:07.890
Everything was great but
I saw a friend's picture

00:08:07.890 --> 00:08:10.690
about having issues getting toilet paper

00:08:10.690 --> 00:08:11.860
and other things.

00:08:11.860 --> 00:08:15.320
I was kind of concerned as to
how this was gonna play out.

00:08:15.320 --> 00:08:18.370
March 14th, the ship received word

00:08:18.370 --> 00:08:21.030
that Chile was planning to close its ports

00:08:21.030 --> 00:08:24.620
to any cruise ship and from then on out,

00:08:24.620 --> 00:08:27.723
that ship was at sea with nowhere to port.

00:08:29.210 --> 00:08:32.150
On March 22nd, the captain
came on the announcement

00:08:32.150 --> 00:08:35.970
and said, we have people
sick with a flu-like illness,

00:08:35.970 --> 00:08:38.040
everybody's gotta be
confided to their quarters.

00:08:38.040 --> 00:08:39.940
The whole ship's going into quarantine.

00:08:39.940 --> 00:08:43.130
From March 22nd was kind of a,

00:08:43.130 --> 00:08:44.710
I guess a different feel.

00:08:44.710 --> 00:08:47.110
Didn't feel like a cruise anymore.

00:08:47.110 --> 00:08:50.160
Sometimes I sat out on the deck at night

00:08:50.160 --> 00:08:52.910
and I would just listen to the waves.

00:08:52.910 --> 00:08:56.500
Now, sadly sometimes I
listened also to a cascade

00:08:56.500 --> 00:08:57.573
of people coughing.

00:08:59.050 --> 00:09:01.360
After everybody was confided to quarters

00:09:01.360 --> 00:09:03.648
for a few days, the captain
came on the announcement

00:09:03.648 --> 00:09:06.560
and said, you know, we're sorry to report

00:09:06.560 --> 00:09:10.000
that four people had passed
away over the last couple days.

00:09:10.000 --> 00:09:13.440
So many crew on the
Zaandam were getting sick,

00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:15.280
that they were having trouble taking care

00:09:15.280 --> 00:09:17.990
of all the passengers, and so
the company made the decision

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:20.560
to bring in another ship
called the Rotterdam.

00:09:20.560 --> 00:09:24.310
And started ferrying passengers,
five, six, 700 passengers

00:09:24.310 --> 00:09:25.860
who seemed to be less sick.

00:09:25.860 --> 00:09:27.820
They put them on the Rotterdam.

00:09:27.820 --> 00:09:30.200
So, now they had two
ships full of passengers

00:09:30.200 --> 00:09:32.033
that could not come to port.

00:09:33.030 --> 00:09:36.160
Panama didn't even want them
to go through the canal.

00:09:36.160 --> 00:09:39.180
Finally, the Panamanian Government decided

00:09:39.180 --> 00:09:41.660
after all to let them go through the canal

00:09:41.660 --> 00:09:42.930
and that's what happened.

00:09:42.930 --> 00:09:45.120
Both their ships passed through the Canal

00:09:45.120 --> 00:09:47.483
and they slowly made
their way back to Florida.

00:09:48.930 --> 00:09:51.210
After days at sea, with
their fate up in the air,

00:09:51.210 --> 00:09:53.280
a pair of Holland America cruise ships

00:09:53.280 --> 00:09:55.340
were given clearance to
dock at Port Everglades

00:09:55.340 --> 00:09:56.986
Thursday afternoon.

00:09:56.986 --> 00:10:00.220
Yay, we're back home.

00:10:00.220 --> 00:10:02.003
Back to the States.

00:10:03.690 --> 00:10:04.650
There were quite a number of people

00:10:04.650 --> 00:10:08.560
that were actually sick and
they were taken to hospitals.

00:10:08.560 --> 00:10:10.850
And of course, they were those
four people who passed away

00:10:10.850 --> 00:10:13.763
that had be taken home,
or find a way home.

00:10:22.470 --> 00:10:26.090
We've gone through
Ebola, Zika, MERs, SARs,

00:10:26.090 --> 00:10:27.600
the industry, because we're global,

00:10:27.600 --> 00:10:29.253
we have to deal with this stuff.

00:10:30.180 --> 00:10:32.660
You know, it's been
devastating, temporarily,

00:10:32.660 --> 00:10:34.900
but the long-term future will be great,

00:10:34.900 --> 00:10:37.320
as long as we all stand together.

00:10:37.320 --> 00:10:39.320
So, since this crisis began,

00:10:39.320 --> 00:10:41.750
Carnival, its business
has really been suffering.

00:10:41.750 --> 00:10:45.670
We've seen its stock really
plummet quickly significantly.

00:10:45.670 --> 00:10:48.860
We spent weeks talking
to company executives

00:10:48.860 --> 00:10:51.960
and the company was really
upbeat and positive,

00:10:51.960 --> 00:10:53.610
if not defiant.

00:10:53.610 --> 00:10:55.770
The CEO, Arnold Donald kept saying,

00:10:55.770 --> 00:10:58.800
look, back when this
affected our first ship,

00:10:58.800 --> 00:11:01.714
the world still hadn't
known about coronavirus yet.

00:11:01.714 --> 00:11:05.310
In his words, it was still a China issue.

00:11:05.310 --> 00:11:06.280
We talked to the CDC,

00:11:06.280 --> 00:11:08.810
we talked to the head of
their Cruise Ship Task Force,

00:11:08.810 --> 00:11:09.990
Dr. Cindy Friedman.

00:11:09.990 --> 00:11:12.450
And she said, that excuse does not fly.

00:11:12.450 --> 00:11:14.260
It would be one thing
if it was only aboard

00:11:14.260 --> 00:11:16.070
the Diamond Princess or
even the Grand Princess,

00:11:16.070 --> 00:11:17.160
those first two ships.

00:11:17.160 --> 00:11:18.830
But the fact that this crisis continued

00:11:18.830 --> 00:11:20.380
to affect Carnival afterward,

00:11:20.380 --> 00:11:23.294
essentially Carnival
should have known better.

00:11:23.294 --> 00:11:25.833
I look forward to cruising again one day.

00:11:26.680 --> 00:11:30.420
But you know, I realized
the paradigm has changed.

00:11:30.420 --> 00:11:32.910
It's very easy to say would
you ever cruise again,

00:11:32.910 --> 00:11:36.500
but I'm wondering, well, what's
the world gonna look like?

00:11:36.500 --> 00:11:38.230
Will we ever be going to concerts,

00:11:38.230 --> 00:11:41.093
sporting events, you know
it's not just cruising.

00:11:43.941 --> 00:11:46.530
One thing that I do agree
with Arnold Donald on,

00:11:46.530 --> 00:11:49.910
he said this is an
unprecedented generational

00:11:49.910 --> 00:11:53.360
global event and I think
that's totally spot on.

00:11:53.360 --> 00:11:55.040
And in the years ahead,
we're gonna look back

00:11:55.040 --> 00:11:57.670
and we're gonna say who
responded to that generational

00:11:57.670 --> 00:11:59.433
crisis well and who did not.

